# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# The point of this file is to let leak detection be on at all. With these
# two quiet, a leak introduced by new code fails the suite instead of
# vanishing into a pile that was already there.
#
# Measured on 2026-09-20, after the spec directory cache was fixed: 51,304
# bytes survive a headless run, and 51,248 of them are the first entry
# below. What is actually ours is 56 bytes.

# ALSA, reached through SDL_native_midi's open_seq. Not ours, allocated once
# when the sequencer opens, and held for the life of the process by design.
# 1,566 allocations of it.
leak:open_seq

# The event handler built in Game::Game, through WindowManager, and never
# deleted: 56 bytes, and the tree under it is still reachable so it is not
# reported. Tearing it down means deciding a shutdown order for code that
# has never had one, which is a task of its own and not a leak fix.
leak:EventHandler::EventHandler
